    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d552">

                <pb facs="0629" n="1307" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1307"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Fogg.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 25.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 19, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of August 28 (No. 21) has
                    been received. It is pleasant to see that while this republic is engaged in so
                    severe a struggle to preserve its existence, the only state in Europe which
                    enjoys such free institutions is contented, peaceful, and prosperous. We are,
                    however, only passing through a trial of which Switzerland has had many painful
                    experiences.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi> G. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Fogg</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        Berne.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
